---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import CopyableCode from "../../components/CopyableCode.astro";
import { InsetText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-solid";
---

<ToolingLayout
  title="Update OpenCode to version 2"
  currentPath="/tooling/opencode-update"
>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Update OpenCode to version 2</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    We are using OpenCode version 2. If you installed OpenCode version 1 you
    need to update your software and configuration file. To do this:
  </p>
  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#check-your-version">
        Check if you need to update
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#prepare-your-config">
        Prepare your config file
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-opencode-v2">
        Install OpenCode v2
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#configure-opencode">
        Configure OpenCode with your old settings
      </a>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These steps work for most setups. If you run into issues you can't resolve,
    contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel on i.AI Slack.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="check-your-version">
    Check if you need to update
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    To check your current OpenCode version, in Terminal, run:
  </p>
  <CopyableCode code="opencode --version" />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If the version number starts with 1, you need to update to version 2.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="prepare-your-config">
    Prepare your config file
  </h2>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To back up your existing config files, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cp -r ~/.config/opencode ~/.config/opencode-v1-backup" />
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/opencode.json" download>
        Download the OpenCode configuration file
      </a>{" "}
      and move it to your Desktop.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">
    Copy your custom settings to the new config file
  </h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you have custom settings (for example, MCP servers), you'll need to copy
    them to the new config file.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To open your old config file, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code ~/.config/opencode-v1-backup/opencode.json" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Find the <code class="app-code">"mcp"</code> section in your old config
      and copy your server definitions, for example:
      <CopyableCode
        code={`"context7": { ... },
"slack": { ... }`}
      />
    </li>
    <li>
      To open your new config file on your Desktop, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code ~/Desktop/opencode.json" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Find the <code class="app-code">"mcp"</code> section and paste your server
      definitions inside the <code class="app-code">"servers"</code> object:
      <CopyableCode
        code={`"mcp": {
  "servers": {
    // paste your servers here
  }
}`}
      />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-opencode-v2">
    Install OpenCode v2
  </h2>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To install the update, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="brew unlink opencode && brew install anomalyco/tap/opencode-v2" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To check the installation was successful, run:
      <CopyableCode code="opencode --version" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If the version number starts with 2, you have successfully installed version
    2. If the version still starts with 1, run the installation command again.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="configure-opencode">
    Configure OpenCode with your old settings
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">To move your updated config file into place, run:</p>
  <CopyableCode code="cp ~/Desktop/opencode.json ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json" />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You'll need to re-authenticate OAuth servers (such as Slack, Atlassian or
    PostHog) on first use. OpenCode v2 will prompt you when authentication is
    needed.
  </p>
</ToolingLayout>
